MONTRÉAL PROJECT DOCS
=====================

This repository is used for continuous deployment of design documents
for the Montréal Project. See https://github.com/ubc-asic/montreal.

The AsciiDoc files are deployed using Github Pages and Antora to
https://ubc-asic.github.io/montreal.

Usage
-----

1.  To add a page, create a new file with the 'adoc' extension under
    'modules/ROOT/pages':

	$ touch modules/ROOT/pages/page.adoc

2.  To list the new page in the navigation (left sidebar on the deployed site),
    link to the page in 'modules/ROOT/nav.adoc':

	modules/ROOT/nav.adoc
	------------------------------------------------------------------------
	* xref:page.adoc[Page Name]
	------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.  To add the page to the header menu, modify the UI template in
    'ui/supplemental_ui/partials/header-content.hbs':

	ui/supplemental_ui/partials/header-content.hbs
	------------------------------------------------------------------------
	<div id="topbar-nav" class="navbar-menu">
	  <div class="navbar-end">
	    <a class="navbar-item" href="/montreal/page.html">Page Name</a>
	  </div>
	</div>
	------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Note that the hyperlink reference is to an 'html' extension, not 'adoc'.

4.  Commit your changes and push to the Github server to trigger the CD action:

	$ git add <modified-files>
	$ git commit -m "Commit message"
	$ git push origin docs
